e is the correct approach.\n843\t\n844\t\n845\t  I will now rewrite copy_book_to_fixture.sh to correctly and dynamically locate the fixture database file using a glob pattern, making it robust and aligned\n846\t  with our best practices.\n847\t\n848\t  Step 3 (Corrected): Refactor copy_book_to_fixture.sh\n849\t\n850\t\n851\t  I will now apply the glob pattern logic to find the fixture database, ensuring the script is resilient and correctly implemented.\n852\t\n853\t�� ✔  WriteFile Writing to ...specs/fixtures/copy_book_to_fixture.sh  �\n854\t��  �\n855\t��  1  #!/bin/zsh  �\n856\t��  2  �\n857\t��  3  - # Script to copy a complete book entry from the real Apple Books database to a specific test fixture.  �\n858\t��  3  + # Copies a complete book entry from the real Apple Books database to a test fixture.  �\n859\t��  4  # Usage: ./copy_book_to_fixture.sh <username> \"<book_title>\"  �\n860\t��  5  �\n861\t��  6  + set -e  �\n862\t��  7  +  �\n863\t��  8  USERNAME=$1  �\n864\t��  9  BOOK_TITLE=$2  �\n865\t��  10  �\n866\t��  13  exit 1  �\n867\t��  14  fi  �\n868\t��  15  �\n869\t��  16  + source \"$(dirname \"$0\")/_common.sh\"  �\n870\t��  17  +  �\n871\t��  18  # --- Define Paths ---  �\n872\t��  15  - # Common path sub-expression for BKLibrary databases  �\n873\t��  16  - BKLIBRARY_CONTAINERS_SUBPATH=\"Library/Containers/com.apple.iBooksX/Data/Documents/BKLibrary\"  �\n874\t��  19  + REAL_DB_PATH=$(find \"$HOME/$BKLIBRARY_USER_SUBPATH\" -name \"BKLibrary-*.sqlite\" | head -n 1)  �\n875\t��  20  + if [[ ! -f \"$REAL_DB_PATH\" ]]; then  �\n876\t��  21  +  echo \"Error: Real Apple Books database not found.\"  �\n877\t��  22  +  exit 1  �\n878\t��  23  + fi  �\n879\t��  24  �\n880\t��  18  - # Path to the real Apple Books database (dynamically found)  �\n881\t��  19  - REAL_DB_PATH=$(find ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.iBooksX/Data/Documents/BKLibrary -name \"BKLibrary-*.sqlite\" | head -n 1)  �\n882\t��  25  + FIXTURE_DIR=\"$PROJECT_ROOT/$BKLIBRARY_FIXTURE_SUBPATH/