\t��  \tclaude-dev-log-diary/day-016.md  �\n4806\t��  \tspecs/apple_books/fixtures/All_Books_20250627.swift  �\n4807\t��  \tspecs/apple_books/fixtures/users/test_reader/Library/Containers/com.apple.iBooksX/Data/Documents/BKLibrary/BKLibrary-fixture.sqlite  �\n4808\t��  �\n4809\t��  �\n4810\t\n4811\t�� Okay, the staged files are correct for this commit.\n4812\t\n4813\t\n4814\t  Here's the proposed commit message for the first commit:\n4815\t\n4816\t\n4817\t\n4818\t   1 feat(docs): Document ZSTATE cloud mapping and fixture management scripts\n4819\t   2\n4820\t   3 This commit documents the research findings for `ZSTATE` values in `BKLibrary.sqlite` and their mapping to \"Cloud\" status in Apple Books UI, as\n4821\t     outlined in the `TODO.md` research backlog. The `docs/apple_books.md` file has been updated with this mapping and relevant UI analysis.\n4822\t   4\n4823\t   5 Additionally, new fixture creation scripts (`copy_book_to_fixture.sh`, `create_fixture.sh`, `_common.sh`) have been added, and the documentation\n4824\t     in `docs/apple_books.md` has been updated to explain their usage for reproducible fixture management. The `TODO.md` file has been updated to\n4825\t     reflect the completion of the ZSTATE research.\n4826\t   6\n4827\t   7 Co-Authored-By: Gemini 2.5 Pro (gemini-2.5-pro) <noreply@google.com>\n4828\t   8 Co-Authored-By: Gemini 2.5 Flash (gemini-2.5-flash) <noreply@google.com>\n4829\t\n4830\t\n4831\t\n4832\t  Would you like me to commit with this message?\n4833\t\n4834\t\n4835\t��  > explain to me the prefix convention, \"feat(docs)\" seems strange, as we didn't implement a feature, we did a research spike as part of our implementation of �\n4836\t��  cloud feature, which will be commited last, we're splitting the commits to tell an easily understandable narattives for future readers of our repo history �\n4837\t\n4838\t\n4839\t�� You're absolutely right to question the prefix and emphasize the narrative in the commit history. My apologies for not fully aligning with that perspective\n4840\t  initially.\n4841\t\n4842\t\n4843\t  The prefix convention, often following Conventional Commits (https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/), aims to provide a clear, machine-readable summary\n4844\t   of the change type.\n4845\t\n4846\t\n4847\t   * feat: A new feature (user-facing functionality).\n4848\t   * fix: A bug fix.\n4849\t   * docs: Documentation only changes.\n4850\t   * chore: Routine tasks, maintenance, or changes to the build process or tooling that don't affect the source code directly.\n4851\t   * refactor: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature.\n4852\t   * test: Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests.\n4853\t\n4854\t\n4855\t  You're correct that this commit isn't implementing a user-facing feature. It's the outcome of a research spike and the introduction of development tooling (the\n4856\t   fixture scripts), along with documentation updates.\n4857\t\n4858\t\n4859\t  Given your goal of telling an easily understandable narrative, and avoiding feat for this, the most appropriate prefix is docs. While the scripts are tooling,\n4860\t  their primary purpose in this commit is to support the documented fixture management process, making them tightly coupled with the documentation.\n4861\t\n4862\t  Here's the revised commit message, focusing on the narrative of completing the research and providing the necessary documentation and tools for fixture\n4863\t  management:\n4864\t\n4865\t\n4866\t\n4867\t   1 docs: Document ZSTATE cloud mapping and fixture management scripts\n4868\t   2\n4869\t   3 This commit documents the research findings for `ZSTATE` values in `BKLibrary.sqlite` and their mapping to \"Cloud\" status in Apple Books UI. This\n4870\t     research was a prerequisite for implementing cloud filtering functionality. The `docs/apple_books.md` file has been updated with this mapping and\n4871\t     relevant UI analysis.\n4872\t   4\n4873\t   5 Additionally, new fixture creation scripts (`_common.sh`, `copy_book_to_fixture.sh`, `create_fixture.sh`) have been added to enable reproducible\n4874\t     test fixture management. The `TODO.md` file has been updated to reflect the completion of the ZSTATE research.\n4875\t   6\n4876\t   7 Co-Authored-By: Gemini 2.5 Pro (gemini-2.5-pro) <noreply@google.com>\n4877\t   8 Co-Authored-By: Gemini 2.5 Flash (gemini-2.5-flash) <noreply@google.com>\n4878\t\n4879\t\n4880\t\n4881\t  Does this revised message and explanation align with your expectations for the narrative?\n4882\t\n4883\t\n4884\t��  > You know what, I think we should first commit changes to the docs only with the ZSTATE as resuts of our research (so we should unstage the lines 210-239  �\n4885\t��  and first go with the ZSTATE research results. Can you do that? We'll then go with chore commit for the fixture scripts and their documentation; then we'll �\n4886\t��  see how to structure the rest of the commits  �\n4887\t\n4888\t\n4889\t�� You're right, that's a much clearer narrative. My apologies for the continued misinterpretation of the commit boundaries.\n4890\t\n4891\t\n4892\t  We will proceed with the following plan for the first commit:\n4893\t   1. Unstage the fixture scripts (_common.sh, copy_book_to_fixture.sh, create_fixture.sh).\n4894\t   2. Revert the documentation for fixture scripts in docs/apple_books.md to its state before I added the comprehensive explanation.\n4895\t   3. Confirm staged files (TODO.md, docs/apple_books.md with only ZSTATE changes, and the image files).\n4896\t   4. Propose the commit message for the ZSTATE research documentation.\n4897\t\n4898\t\n4899\t  Let's start by unstaging the fixture scripts.\n4900\t\n4901\t�� ✔  Shell git restore --staged specs/apple_books/fixtures/_common.sh specs/apple_books/fixtures/copy_book_to_fixture.sh specs/apple_books/fixtures/create_fi…  �\n4902\t\n4903\t�� Now, I will revert the documentation for fixture scripts in docs/apple_books.md to its previous state.\n490