oks.md` and the image files.\n5456\t   3. Confirm staged files using git status.\n5457\t   4. Propose the commit message.\n5458\t\n5459\t\n5460\t\n5461\t\n5462\t\n5463\t\n5464\t  Let's start by restoring docs/apple_books.md to its correct content.\n5465\t\n5466\t\n5467\t�� Request cancelled.\n5468\t\n5469\t\n5470\t\n5471\t��  > Please recall from your context the last version the file @docs/apple_books.md that contains the full documentation of the ZSTATE research and also the  �\n5472\t��  documentation of the fixture scripts. We are looking for the document state before you said:  �\n5473\t��  > Now, I will revert the documentation for fixture scripts in docs/apple_books.md to its previous state.  �\n5474\t��  �\n5475\t��  Then restore the apple_books.md content to that version!  �\n5476\t\n5477\t\n5478\t\n5479\t�� ✔  ReadManyFiles Will attempt to read and concatenate files using patterns: `docs/apple_books.md` (within target directory: `/Users/palimondo/Developer/Boo…  �\n5480\t��  �\n5481\t��  ### ReadManyFiles Result (Target Dir: `/Users/palimondo/Developer/BookMinder`)  �\n5482\t��  �\n5483\t��  Successfully read and concatenated content from **1 file(s)**.  �\n5484\t��  �\n5485\t��  **Processed Files:**  �\n5486\t��  - `docs/apple_books.md`  �\n5487\t\n5488\t�� You are absolutely right. My deepest apologies for the repeated failures and for causing such frustration. I understand the critical importance of\n5489\t  maintaining the correct file content and commit history.\n5490\t\n5491\t\n5492\t  I will now recall the exact content of docs/apple_books.md that includes both the ZSTATE documentation and the comprehensive fixture scripts documentation,\n5493\t  as it was before my erroneous revert. I will then restore the file to that precise version.\n5494\t\n5495\t\n5496\t  Here is the content I will restore docs/apple_books.md to:\n5497\t\n5498\t\n5499\t\n5500\t    1 # Apple Books Data Sources\n5501\t    2\n5502\t    3 This document describes the data sources used by Apple Books on macOS and how BookMinder accesses them.\n5503\t    4\n5504\t    5 ## Overview\n5505\t    6\n5506\t    7 Apple Books stores data across multiple files and databases in different container directories. Understanding these data sources is crucial for\n5507\t      extracting book metadata, reading progress, and activity information.\n5508\t    8\n5509\t    9 ## Container Directories\n5510\t   10\n5511\t   11 Apple Books uses sandboxed containers to store its data:\n5512\t   12\n5513\t   13 - **com.apple.BKAgentService**: Contains the book files and basic catalog\n5514\t   14 - **com.apple.iBooksX**: Contains databases for reading progress, activity, and UI state\n5515\t   15\n5516\t   16 ## Data Sources\n5517\t   17\n5518\t   18 ### 1. Books.plist\n5519\t   19\n5520\t   20 **Location**: `/Users/{user}/Library/Containers/com.apple.BKAgentService/Data/Documents/iBooks/Books/Books.plist`\n5521\t   21\n5522\t   22 **Purpose**: Primary book catalog with metadata\n5523\t   23\n5524\t   24 **Key Fields**:\n5525\t   25 - `itemName`: Book title\n5526\t   26 - `artistName`: Author name\n5527\t   27 - `path`: Relative path to EPUB file\n5528\t   28 - `updateDate`: Last modification date\n5529\t   29 - `BKPercentComplete`: Only present for **finished books** (always 1.0 = 100%)\n5530\t   30\n5531\t   31 **Important Discovery**:\n5532\t   32 - Contains all books in library (179 total in test case)\n5533\t   33 - Only 22 books have `BKPercentComplete` field (12% of library)\n5534\t   34 - All books with `BKPercentComplete` show 1.0 (100% complete)\n5535\t   35 - Books without this field are either unread or partially read\n5536\t   36 - **Does NOT contain actual reading progress for books in progress**\n5537\t   37\n5538\t   38 ### 2. BKLibrary SQLite Database\n5539\t   39\n5540\t   40 **Location Pattern**: `/Users/{user}/Library/Containers/com.apple.iBooksX/Data/Documents/BKLibrary/BKLibrary-*.sqlite`\n5541\t   41\n5542\t   42 **Note**: The filename contains variable numbers (e.g., `BKLibrary-1-091020131601.sqlite`) that change between installations. Use glob pattern\n5543\t      matching to locate.\n5544\t   43\n5545\t   44 **Purpose**: Complete library database with reading progress and activity\n5546\t   45\n5547\t   46 **Key Table**: `ZBKLIBRARYASSET`\n5548\t   47\n5549\t   48 **Critical Fields for Reading Progress**:\n5550\t   49 - `ZTITLE`: Book title\n5551\t   50 - `ZAUTHOR`: Author name\n5552\t   51 - `ZASSETID`: Asset identifier (matches Books.plist keys)\n5553\t   52 - `ZREADINGPROGRESS`: Float value (0.0 to 1.0) representing actual reading progress\n5554\t   53 - `ZLASTOPENDATE`: Timestamp when book was last opened (Apple reference date)\n5555\t   54 - `ZISFINISHED`: Integer indicating if book is finished (1 = finished, 0 = not finished)\n5556\t   55 - `ZDATEFINISHED`: Timestamp when book was finished\n5557\t   56 - `ZCREATIONDATE`: When book was added to library\n5558\t   57\n5559\t   58 **Additional Important Fields**:\n5560\t   59 - `ZISSAMPLE`: Integer indicating if book is a sample (1 = sample, 0 = full book)\n5561\t   60 - `ZCONTENTTYPE`: Integer indicating content type (likely: 1 = Book, 3 = PDF)\n5562\t   61 - `ZPATH`: Path to the book file (relative to Books directory)\n5563\t   62 - `ZFILESIZE`: Size of the book file in bytes\n5564\t   63 - `ZSTATE`: Integer indicating download/availability state\n5565\t   64 - `ZGENRE`: Book genre/category\n5566\t   65 - `ZKIND`: Content kind (e.g., \"ebook\", \"pdf\")\n5567\t   66 - `ZPAGECOUNT`: Number of pages in the book\n5568\t   67 - `ZISEPHEMERAL`: Integer indicating temporary status\n5569\t   68\n5570\t   69 **Example Query for Recent Books**:\n5571\t\n5572\t  SELECT ZTITLE, ZAUTHOR, ZREADINGPROGRESS, ZLASTOPENDATE, ZISFINISHED\n5573\t  FROM ZBKLIBRARYASSET\n5574\t  WHERE ZREADINGPROGRESS > 0\n5575\t  ORDER BY ZLASTOPENDATE DESC\n5576\t  LIMIT 10;\n5577\t\n5578\t\n5579\t    1\n5580\t    2 **Sample Results**:\n5581\t    3 - \"The Left Hand of Darkness\" - Ursula K. Le Guin - 32% progress\n5582\t    4 - \"Lao Tzu: Tao Te Ching\" - Ursula K. Le Guin - 8% progress\n5583\t    5 - \"The Beginning of Infinity\" - David Deutsch - 59% progress\n5584\t    6\n5585\t    7 ### 3. Recently Opened Books Database\n5586\t    8\n5587\t    9 **Location**: `/Users/{user}/Library/Containers/com.apple.iBooksX/Data/Documents/BCRecentlyOpenedBooksDB/BCRecentlyOpenedBooksDB.sqlite`\n5588\t   10\n5589\t   11 **Note**: This filename appears to be fixed (no variable numbers).\n5590\t   12\n5591\t   13 **Purpose**: Tracks reading sessions and activity\n5592\t   14\n5593\t   15 **Key Table**: `ZBCASSETREADINGSESSION`\n5594\t   16\n5595\t   17 **Fields**:\n5596\t   18 - `ZASSETID`: Asset identifier\n5597\t   19 - `ZTIMEOPENED`: When reading session started (Apple reference date)\n5598\t   20 - `ZTIMECLOSED`: When reading session ended\n5599\t   21 - `ZTIMEUPDATED`: Last update timestamp\n5600\t   22\n5601\t   23 ## Data Relationships\n5602\t   24\n5603\t   25 ### Asset ID Mapping\n5604\t   26 - Books.plist uses keys like \"401429854\" (numeric strings)\n5605\t   27 - BKLibrary database uses same IDs in `ZASSETID` field\n5606\t   28 - Reading sessions reference same IDs in `ZASSETID`\n5607\t   29\n5608\t   30 ### Progress Data Sources Hierarchy\n5609\t   31 1. **BKLibrary.sqlite** - Authoritative source for reading progress (ZREADINGPROGRESS 0.0-1.0)\n5610\t   32 2. **Books.plist** - Only shows finished books (BKPercentComplete = 1.0)\n5611\t   33 3. **Reading sessions** - Activity timestamps but no progress percentages\n5612\t   34\n5613\t   35 ### Content Type Identification\n5614\t   36\n5615\t   37 **In BKLibrary Database**:\n5616\t   38 - `ZCONTENTTYPE = 1`: Regular books (EPUB)\n5617\t   39 - `ZCONTENTTYPE = 3`: PDF documents\n5618\t   40 - `ZISSAMPLE = 1`: Sample/preview books\n5619\t   41 - `ZKIND = \"ebook\"`: Standard ebook format\n5620\t   42 - `ZKIND = \"pdf\"`: PDF document\n5621\t   43\n5622\t   44 **In Books.plist**:\n5623\t   45 - `kind = \"ebook\"`: EPUB books\n5624\t   46 - `fileExtension = \"epub\"`: EPUB format\n5625\t   47 - `BKBookType = \"epub\"`: Book type identifier\n5626\t   48\n5627\t   49 ### Asset ID Correlation System\n5628\t   50\n5629\t   51 Asset IDs provide the link between different data sources:\n5630\t   52\n5631\t   53 **Format**: Numeric strings (e.g., \"401429854\", \"1296850431\")\n5632\t   54\n5633\t   55 **Cross-Reference Pattern**:\n5634\t\n5635\t  Books.plist key: \"401429854\"\n5636\t��\n5637\t  BKLibrary.ZASSETID: \"401429854\"\n5638\t��\n5639\t  Reading Session.ZASSETID: \"401429854\"\n5640\t��\n5641\t  File path: \"401429854.epub\"\n5642\t\n5643\t\n5644\t    1\n5645\t    2 **Asset ID Sources**:\n5646\t    3 - iTunes Store ID for purchased books\n5647\t    4 - Generated ID for sideloaded content\n5648\t    5 - Hexadecimal IDs for some system content (e.g., \"1F150082C5E6CD9413FAA197989BC910\")\n5649\t    6\n5650\t    7 ### Apple Timestamp Format Details\n5651\t    8\n5652\t    9 Apple uses Core Data timestamp format with reference date January 1, 2001, 00:00:00 UTC.\n5653\t   10\n5654\t   11 **Conversion Examples**:\n5655\t\n5656\t  Raw timestamp: 772198715.562895\n5657\t  Converts to: 2025-06-22 20:11:55 UTC\n5658\t\n5659\t\n5660\t  def apple_to_unix_timestamp(apple_timestamp):\n5661\t  Apple epoch: January 1, 2001 UTC\n5662\t  Unix epoch: January 1, 1970 UTC\n5663\t  Difference: 978307200 seconds (31 years)\n5664\t      return apple_timestamp + 978307200\n5665\t\n5666\t\n5667\t  def apple_timestamp_to_datetime(apple_timestamp):\n5668\t      apple_epoch = datetime.datetime(2001, 1, 1, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)\n5669\t      return apple_epoch + datetime.timedelta(seconds=apple_timestamp)\n5670\t\n5671\t\n5672\t    1\n5673\t    2 **Common Timestamp Fields**:\n5674\t    3 - `ZLASTOPENDATE`: When book was last opened\n5675\t    4 - `ZDATEFINISHED`: When book was completed\n5676\t    5 - `ZCREATIONDATE`: When book was added to library\n5677\t    6 - `updateDate` (Books.plist): Last modification (ISO format)\n5678\t    7\n5679\t    8 ### Database Performance and Access\n5680\t    9\n5681\t   10 **File Structure**:\n5682\t   11 - Main database: `BKLibrary-*.sqlite`\n5683\t   12 - Write-Ahead Log: `BKLibrary-*.sqlite-wal`\n5684\t   13 - Shared Memory: `BKLibrary-*.sqlite-shm`\n5685\t   14\n5686\t   15 **Access Pattern**:\\n- Query the main `.sqlite` file\\n- SQLite automatically handles WAL/SHM files\\n- Database may be locked during active Apple\n5687\t      Books usage\\n\\n**Recommended Query Approach**:\\n```python\\nimport sqlite3\\nimport glob\\n\\n# Locate database\\npattern =\n5688\t      f\\\"{home}/Library/Containers/com.apple.iBooksX/Data/Documents/BKLibrary/BKLibrary-*.sqlite\\\"\\ndb_files = glob.glob(pattern)\\nif not db_files:\\n\n5689\t      raise FileNotFoundError(\\\"BKLibrary database not found\\\")\\n\\ndb_path = db_files[0]  # Use first match\\n\\n# Query with error handling\\ntry:\\n\n5690\t      with sqlite3.connect(db_path) as conn:\\n  conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row  # Enable column access by name\\n  cursor = conn.cursor()\\n\n5691\t      # Execute queries...\\nexcept sqlite3.OperationalError as e:\\n  if \\\"database is locked\\\" in str(e):\\n  # Apple Books is running, retry or\n5692\t      prompt user\\n  pass\\n\n5693\t\n5694\t  ``\\n\\n### Copying Book Entries to Test Fixtures\\n\\nTo ensure test fixtures accurately reflect real-world data and simplify test case creation, you can copy\n5695\t  complete book entries from your main Apple Books database to a test fixture database. This method is robust as it directly transfers data between two SQLite\n5696\t   databases with identical schemas.\\n\\nThe fixture management involves two primary scripts located in specs/apple_books/fixtures/`:\\n\\n1.\n5697\t  **`create_fixture.sh**: This script creates a fresh, empty test fixture database for a specified user. It extracts the schema from your real Apple Books\n5698\t  database to ensure consistency.\\n  ``zsh\\n  ./specs/apple_books/fixtures/create_fixture.sh <username>\\n  \\n  Example:\\n  zsh\\n\n5699\t  ./specs/apple_books/fixtures/create_fixture.sh test_reader\\n\n5700\t  ``\\n  This will create a BKLibrary-fixture.sqlite file within the test_reader` user\\'s fixture directory.\\n\\n2.  **`copy_book_to_fixture.sh**: After\n5701\t  creating a fixture, this script allows you to copy specific book entries from your real Apple Books database into the newly created fixture database. It\n5702\t  dynamically extracts all column names to ensure a complete and accurate copy.\\n  ``zsh\\n  ./specs/apple_books/fixtures/copy_book_to_fixture.sh\n5703\t  <username> \\\"<book_title>\\\"\\n  ```\\n  Example:\\n  ```zsh\\n  ./specs/apple_books/fixtures/copy_book_to_fixture.sh test_reader \\\"The Left Hand of\n5704\t  Darkness\\\"\\n\n5705\t  ``\\n\\nBoth scripts utilize _common.sh` for shared path definitions.\\n\\nThis process ensures that your test fixtures are isolated, reproducible, and\n5706\t  accurately reflect the structure and data of your live Apple Books environment.\\n\\n\\n## Apple Books UI Analysis\\n\\n### UI Structure Overview\\n\\nApple Books\n5707\t  organizes content in the Home screen with distinct sections that correlate directly to database states:\\n\\n1. **Continue Section**: Currently reading books\n5708\t  (progress 1-99%)\\n2. **Previous Section**: All previously accessed books (mixed states)\\n3. **Books Read This Year**: Achievement view (finished books\n5709\t  only)\\n\\n### Content Types and Indicators\\n\\n**Content Types**:\\n- **Book**: Regular ebooks (EPUB format)\\n- **PDF**: Technical documents, manuals,\n5710\t  papers\\n- **Sample**: Free previews from the bookstore\\n\\n**Status Indicators**:\\n- **Percentage (1%-99%)**: Active reading progress\\n- **\\\"Finished\\\" +\n5711\t  blue checkmark**: Completed books (100%)\\n- **\\\"Sample\\\"**: Preview/trial versions\\n- **Cloud icon**: Books stored in iCloud but not downloaded\n5712\t  locally\\n\\n### Detailed Section Analysis\\n\\n#### Continue Section (10 books visible)\\nBooks currently being read, sorted by recent activity. All show\n5713\t  percentage progress:\\n\\n| Title | Author | Progress | Type | Cloud |\\n|-------|--------|----------|------|-------|\\n| The Left Hand of Darkness | Ursula K.\n5714\t  Le Guin & Charlie Jane Anders | 32% | Book | No |\\n| Lao Tzu: Tao Te Ching | Ursula K. Le Guin | 8% | Book | Yes |\\n| Tao Te Ching | Laozi | 3% | Book | Yes\n5715\t   |\\n| Quicksilver | Neal Stephenson | 4% | Book | Yes |\\n| The Beginning of Infinity | David Deutsch | 59% | Book | No |\\n| User Story Mapping | Jeff Patton\n5716\t   | 21% | Book | No |\\n| Growing Object-Oriented Software, Guided by Tests | Steve Freeman | 8% | Book | No |\\n| A Clockwork Orange | Anthony Burgess | 1% |\n5717\t  Book | No |\\n| The Canon of Reason and Virtue | Paul Carus Daisetsu... | 14% | Book | Yes |\\n| record-layer-paper | Christos Chrysa... | 1% | PDF | Yes\n5718\t  |\\n\\n#### Previous Section\\nMixed collection of all previously accessed books with various states.\\n\\n![Previous Section - List\n5719\t  View](Previous%20list.jpg)\\n![Previous Section - List View Page 2](Previous%20list%20p2.jpg)\\n![Previous Section - Tile\n5720\t  View](Previous%20tiles.jpg)\\n\\n**Partial Progress Books**:\\n- Tiny Experiments - Anne-Laure Le Cunff (1%) Book • Sample\\n- Manual_Melitta_Purista_CZ_SK -\n5721\t  ZINDEL AG (83%) PDF\\n- Mechanický pomaranč - Anthony Burgess (4%) Book\\n- A Clockwork Orange - Anthony Burgess & Andrew Biswell (96%) Book\\n- Quicksilver -\n5722\t  Neal Stephenson (4%) Book • Cloud\\n- Twelve Tomorrows - Neil Stephenson, David Brin, etc. (4%) Book • Cloud\\n- The Scaling Era - Dwarkesh Patel (1%) Book\\n-\n5723\t   Automobil v podnikaní režimy a tipy Ľudskou Rečou sk v2023 - Unknown Author (4%) PDF • Cloud\\n- Working Effectively with Legacy Code - Michael C. Feathers\n5724\t  (2%) Book\\n- Refactoring - Martin Fowler (2%) Book\\n- Extreme Programming Explained - Kent Beck & Cynthia Andres (69%) Book\\n- REST in Practice - Jim\n5725\t  Webber, Savas Parastatidis, and Ian Robinson (5%) Book\\n- Stubborn Attachments - Tyler Cowen (4%) Book\\n\\n**Finished Books**:\\n- MELITTA CAFFEO SOLO -\n5726\t  Unknown Author PDF • Finished\\n- Artificial Intelligence - Tim Rocktäschel Book • Finished\\n- The Coming Wave - Mustafa Suleyman & Michael Bhaskar Book •\n5727\t  Finished\\n- Attack Surface - Cory Doctorow Book • Finished\\n- Red Team Blues - Cory Doctorow Book • Finished\\n\\n**Sample Books**:\\n- Snow Crash - Neal\n5728\t  Stephenson Book • Sample\\n- What\\'s Our Problem? - Tim Urban Book • Sample • Cloud\\n\\n**No Progress Shown**:\\n- Postman - Technopoly - Neil Postman PDF\\n-\n5729\t  For The Win - Cory Doctorow Book\\n\\n#### Books Read This Year Section (4 books)\\nAchievement-focused view showing only completed books:\\n- Attack Surface -\n5730\t  Cory Doctorow\\n- Red Team Blues - Cory Doctorow\\n- Chip War - Chris Miller  \\n- The Diamond Age - Neal Stephenson\\n\\n**Status**: \\\"Yearly Goal Achieved - 4\n5731\t  books finished. Keep reading!\\\"\\n\\n### Database to UI Mapping\\n\\n#### Continue Section = Recent Reading Activity\\n**Database Query**:\\n```sql\\nSELECT * FROM\n5732\t   ZBKLIBRARYASSET \\nWHERE ZREADINGPROGRESS > 0 AND ZREADINGPROGRESS < 1.0\\nORDER BY ZLASTOPENDATE DESC \\nLIMIT 10;\\n```\\n\\n#### Previous Section = All\n5733\t  Library Content\\n**Database Query**:\\n```sql\\nSELECT * FROM ZBKLIBRARYASSET \\nORDER BY ZLASTOPENDATE DESC;\\n```\\n\\n#### Books Read This Year = Finished\n5734\t  Books\\n**Database Query**:\\n```sql\\nSELECT * FROM ZBKLIBRARYASSET \\nWHERE ZISFINISHED = 1 \\nAND ZDATEFINISHED >= [start_of_year_timestamp]\\nORDER BY\n5735\t  ZDATEFINISHED DESC;\\n\n5736\t  ``\\n\\n### Validation Test Cases\\n\\nUse these specific books to validate database queries match UI display:\\n\\n**Top 3 Continue Section Books**:\\n1. \\\"The\n5737\t  Left Hand of Darkness\\\" → Should show ~32% progress\\n2. \\\"Lao Tzu: Tao Te Ching\\\" → Should show ~8% progress  \\n3. \\\"Tao Te Ching\\\" → Should show ~3%\n5738\t  progress\\n\\n**Sample Books** (should have special handling):\\n- \\\"Tiny Experiments\\\" → Sample with 1% progress\\n- \\\"Snow Crash\\\" → Sample with no progress\n5739\t  shown\\n- \\\"What\\'s Our Problem?\\\" → Sample with no progress shown\\n\\n**Finished Books** (should appear in year view):\\n- \\\"Attack Surface\\\", \\\"Red Team\n5740\t  Blues\\\", \\\"Chip War\\\", \\\"The Diamond Age\\\"\\n\\n**PDF Content**:\\n- \\\"Manual_Melitta_Purista_CZ_SK\\\" → 83% progress\\n- \\\"record-layer-paper\\\" → 1%\n5741\t  progress\\n- \\\"MELITTA CAFFEO SOLO\\\" → Finished\\n- \\\"Postman - Technopoly\\\" → No progress\\n\\n**High Progress Books**:\\n- \\\"A Clockwork Orange\\\" (Anthony\n5742\t  Burgess & Andrew Biswell) → 96%\\n- \\\"Reentry\\\" → 82%\\n- \\\"Extreme Programming Explained\\\" → 69%\\n\\n### UI Behavior Insights\\n\\n1. **Continue section\n5743\t  prioritizes active reading** (1-99% progress, recent activity)\\n2. **Previous section shows reading history** (all states, sorted by last access)\\n3.\n5744\t  **Cloud status affects availability** but not progress tracking\\n4. **Sample books can show progress** but are marked distinctly\\n5. **PDF documents\n5745\t  integrate seamlessly** with book progress tracking\\n6. **Finished books appear in multiple sections** (Previous + Year view)\\n7. **Zero progress books\n5746\t  still appear in Previous** if accessed before\\n\\n## Implementation Strategy for \\\"Recent Books\\\"\\n\\nTo implement bookminder list recent with accurate\n5747\t  progress percentages:\\n\\n### Step 1: Locate Database\\n``python\\nimport glob\\ndb_pattern =\n5748\t  f\\\"{home}/Library/Containers/com.apple.iBooksX/Data/Documents/BKLibrary/BKLibrary-*.sqlite\\\"\\ndb_path = glob.glob(pattern)[0]  # Get first match\\n\\n\\n###\n5749\t  Step 2: Query Reading Progress\\nsql\\nSELECT \\n  ZTITLE,\\n  ZAUTHOR, \\n  ZREADINGPROGRESS * 100 as PROGRESS_PERCENT,\\n  ZLASTOPENDATE\\nFROM\n5750\t  ZBKLIBRARYASSET \\nWHERE ZREADINGPROGRESS > 0 \\nORDER BY ZLASTOPENDATE DESC \\nLIMIT 10;\\n\n5751\t  \\n\\n### Step 3: Convert Apple Timestamps\\nApple uses reference date of January 1, 2001 (Core Data timestamp format).\\n\\npython\\nimport datetime\\ndef\n5752\t  apple_timestamp_to_datetime(timestamp):\\n  apple_epoch = datetime.datetime(2001, 1, 1)\\n  return apple_epoch +\n5753\t  datetime.timedelta(seconds=timestamp)\\n\\n\\n### Step 4: Format Output\\n\\nThe Left Hand of Darkness - Ursula K. Le Guin (32%)\\nLao Tzu: Tao Te Ching - Ursula\n5754\t  K. Le Guin (8%)\\nThe Beginning of Infinity - David Deutsch (59%)\\n\n5755\t  ``\\n\\n## User State Scenarios\\n\\nThrough real-world testing on macOS, we discovered distinct Apple Books states for different users:\\n\\n### 1. Never Opened\n5756\t  Apple Books\\n**Containers Present**: \\n- com.apple.iBooksX (created automatically by macOS)\\n- No com.apple.BKAgentService container\\n\\n**Files Present**:\n5757\t  None\\n\\n**Key Insight**: The iBooksX container is created during user account setup, not when Apple Books is first opened.\\n\\n### 2. Fresh Apple Books (Just\n5758\t   Opened, No Books)\\n**Containers Present**: Both containers exist\\n- com.apple.BKAgentService (created when Apple Books first launches)\\n-\n5759\t  com.apple.iBooksX\\n\\n**Files Present**:\\n- Books.plist with empty books array\\n- BKLibrary-.sqlite` database with 0 rows in ZBKLIBRARYASSET table\\n\\nKey\n5760\t  Insight: Apple Books creates all infrastructure immediately upon first launch, including the SQLite database.\\n\\n### 3. Legacy/Edge Case\n5761\t  Installation\\nExample: User \\\"katka\\\" from testing\\n- Containers from 2020-2021\\n- Has `Books.plist` (empty)\\n- Missing `BKLibrary` directory\n5762\t  entirely\\n\\nPossible Causes:\\n- Older Apple Books version\\n- Migration issues\\n- Manual cleanup\\n\\n### 4. Active Reader\\nAll infrastructure present with\n5763\t  actual book data and reading progress.\\n\\n## Database Discovery Timeline\\n\\nThis information was discovered through systematic investigation:\\n\\n1. Initial\n5764\t  Books.plist analysis: Found only completed books (BKPercentComplete)\\n2. Apple Books UI screenshots: Revealed granular progress tracking (1-99%)\\n3. File\n5765\t  system exploration: Located SQLite databases in iBooksX container\\n4. Database schema analysis: Found ZREADINGPROGRESS field with float values\\n5. Data\n5766\t  correlation: Confirmed BKLibrary.sqlite as authoritative progress source\\n6. Filename pattern discovery: Identified variable numbers in database names\\n7.\n5767\t  User state validation: Tested multiple user accounts to understand container creation\\n\\n## Edge Cases and Special Considerations\\n\\n### Progress Edge\n5768\t  Cases\\n- Zero progress books: May exist in library but never opened (ZREADINGPROGRESS = 0.0)\\n- Null progress: Some books may have NULL progress values\\n-\n5769\t  Finished books: Always show ZREADINGPROGRESS = 1.0 AND ZISFINISHED = 1\\n- Sample books: Can have partial progress but remain samples (ZISSAMPLE = 1)\\n\\n###\n5770\t  Content Type Edge Cases  \\n- Mixed format books: Some books may have mismatched file extensions\\n- System content: Hexadecimal asset IDs for system/default\n5771\t  content\\n- Corrupted entries: Books with missing file paths or invalid metadata\\n- iCloud books: Books in cloud but not downloaded locally (check\n5772\t  ZSTATE)\\n\\n### Timestamp Edge Cases\\n- Null timestamps: Books may have NULL values for ZLASTOPENDATE\\n- Future timestamps: Possible due to timezone issues\n5773\t  or system clock problems\\n- Zero timestamps: Apple epoch (2001-01-01) indicates unset values\\n\\n### Database Access Issues\\n- Missing databases: User\n5774\t  hasn\\'t used Apple Books, fresh installation\\n- Permission errors: Sandboxing restrictions, SIP protections\\n- Database locks: Apple Books actively using\n5775\t  database\\n- Schema changes: Apple Books updates may modify database structure\\n- Multiple versions: User might have multiple BKLibrary databases\\n\\n###\n5776\t  Sample Book Handling\\n```sql\\n-- Get samples separately as they behave differently\\nSELECT  FROM ZBKLIBRARYASSET \\nWHERE ZISSAMPLE = 1 \\nAND\n5777\t  ZREADINGPROGRESS > 0\\nORDER BY ZLASTOPENDATE DESC;\\n\\n\\n### Content Filtering Strategies\\nsql\\n-- Active reading (excluding samples and finished)\\nSELECT\n5778\t  FROM ZBKLIBRARYASSET \\nWHERE ZREADINGPROGRESS > 0 \\nAND ZREADINGPROGRESS < 1.0 \\nAND (ZISSAMPLE IS NULL OR ZISSAMPLE = 0)\\nORDER BY ZLASTOPENDATE\n5779\t  DESC;\\n\\n-- Include samples in recent reading  \\nSELECT  FROM ZBKLIBRARYASSET \\nWHERE ZREADINGPROGRESS > 0\\nORDER BY ZLASTOPENDATE DESC;\\n\\n-- Only finished\n5780\t   books this year\\nSELECT * FROM ZBKLIBRARYASSET \\nWHERE ZISFINISHED = 1 \\nAND ZDATEFINISHED > [year_start_timestamp]\\nORDER BY ZDATEFINISHED DESC;\\n\n5781\t\n5782\t  ``\\n\\n## Critical Implementation Notes\\n\\n- **Use glob patterns** for database discovery (filenames contain variable numbers)\\n- **BKLibrary.sqlite is\n5783\t  authoritative** for reading progress, not Books.plist\\n- **Reading progress stored as float** (0.0 to 1.0), multiply by 100 for percentages\\n- **Use\n5784\t  ZLASTOPENDATE for recency**, not updateDate from Books.plist\\n- **Apple timestamps** use 2001-01-01 as epoch, not Unix epoch\\n- **Database files include\n5785\t  WAL/SHM** files (Write-Ahead Logging) - query main .sqlite file\\n- **Handle NULL values** gracefully in all timestamp and progress fields\\n- **Check\n5786\t  ZISSAMPLE flag** to identify preview/trial books\\n- **Use ZCONTENTTYPE** to distinguish between books and PDFs\\n- **Implement retry logic** for database\n5787\t  lock errors\\n- **Validate asset ID format** before cross-referencing with Books.plist\\n\\n## Future Considerations\\n\\n- Monitor for database schema changes\n5788\t  across Apple Books versions\\n- Consider reading session data for more detailed activity analysis\\n- Handle potential permission issues accessing sandboxed\n5789\t  containers\\n- Test across different macOS versions and Apple Books versions\\n\\n# BookMinder Domain Language and CLI Mapping\\n\\nTo ensure clarity and\n5790\t  consistency in BookMinder\\'s development and user interface, we define the following domain language, directly mapped to Apple Books\\' internal data\n5791\t  structures.\\n\\n## 1. Content Type (What is it?)\\n\\nDescribes the fundamental format or origin of the content.\\n\\n-  **Book (EPUB):** A standard e-book,\n5792\t  typically from the Apple Books store or sideloaded.\\n  -  *Mapping:* BKLibrary.sqlite where ZCONTENTTYPE = 1 or ZKIND = \\\"ebook\\\".\\n-  **PDF:** A\n5793\t  Portable Document Format file.\\n  -  *Mapping:* BKLibrary.sqlite where ZCONTENTTYPE = 3 or ZKIND = \\\"pdf\\\".\\n-  **Audiobook:** (Future content type if\n5794\t  data becomes available).\\n\\n## 2. Reading Status (Where am I with it?)\\n\\nDescribes the user\\'s progress through the content. This is a critical aspect for\n5795\t  filtering and display.\\n\\n-  **Finished:** The book is marked as complete by Apple Books.\\n  -  *Mapping:* BKLibrary.sqlite where ZISFINISHED = 1.\\n\n5796\t  -  *Note:* Empirical research shows that ZREADINGPROGRESS may or may not be 1.0 for finished books. However, if ZREADINGPROGRESS is 1.0, then ZISFINISHED\n5797\t  is also 1.\\n-  **In Progress:** The book has some reading progress but is not marked as finished.\\n  -  *Mapping:* BKLibrary.sqlite where\n5798\t  ZREADINGPROGRESS > 0.0 AND ZISFINISHED = 0.\\n-  **Not Started:** The book has 0% reading progress and is not marked as finished.\\n  -  *Mapping:*\n5799\t  BKLibrary.sqlite where ZREADINGPROGRESS = 0.0 AND ZISFINISHED = 0.\\n\\n## 3. Attributes/Flags (Other characteristics?)\\n\\nAdditional properties that can\n5800\t  apply to any content type or reading status.\\n\\n-  **Sample:** A preview version of a book.\\n  -  *Mapping:* BKLibrary.sqlite where ZISSAMPLE = 1.\\n-\n5801\t  **Cloud:** The book is stored in iCloud and not fully downloaded locally.\\n  -  *Mapping:* BKLibrary.sqlite where ZSTATE indicates cloud/local status.\\n\n5802\t     -  *Verified ZSTATE Mappings:*\\n  - ZSTATE = 3: **Cloud Book**. The book is stored in iCloud.\\n  - ZSTATE = 6: **Cloud Sample**. The book is\n5803\t   a sample stored in iCloud.\\n  - ZSTATE = 1: **Local Book**. The book is stored on the device. This includes local samples (where ZISSAMPLE = 1).\\n\n5804\t       - ZSTATE = 5: **Series Entity / Unowned Series Book**. This ZSTATE value is associated with:\\n  - The **series entity itself** (e.g.,\n5805\t  \\\"Hainish\\\"), where ZTITLE matches the series name.\\n  - **Unowned books within a series** (e.g., \\\"Five Ways to Forgiveness\\\"), where ZTITLE is\n5806\t  the individual book title.\\n  Both are linked to individual books via ZSERIESID.\\n\\n## CLI Mapping (Proposed Commands)\\n\\nThis section outlines how\n5807\t  the domain language translates into user-facing CLI commands.\\n\\n-  **bookminder list (Default: recent):** Shows \\\"In Progress\\\" books, ordered by\n5808\t  ZLASTOPENDATE, limited to 10.\\n-  **bookminder list all:** Shows all books in the library, regardless of reading status, ordered by ZLASTOPENDATE. (Maps to\n5809\t   Apple Books \\\"Previous Section\\\").\\n-  **Filtering by Reading Status (--status option):**\\n  -  bookminder list --status finished\\n  -  bookminder\n5810\t  list --status not-started\\n  -  bookminder list --status in-progress\\n-  **Filtering by Content Type (--type option):**\\n  -  bookminder list --type\n5811\t  book\\n  -  bookminder list --type pdf\\n-  **Filtering by Attributes (--flag option):**\\n  -  bookminder list --flag sample`\n5812\t       - bookminder list --flag cloud\n5813\t   - Filtering by Time (`--year` option):\n5814\t       - bookminder list --year <YYYY> (e.g., 2024, current)\n5815\t   - Pagination (`--limit`, `--offset`):\n5816\t       - bookminder list all --limit 20\n5817\t       - bookminder list all --offset 20 --limit 20\n5818\t\n5819\t   1\n5820\t\n5821\t  I will now use write_file to restore docs/apple_books.md to this exact content.\n5822\t\n5823\t�� Request cancelled.\n5824\t\n5825\t\n5826\t\n5827\t��  > Try again to restore docs/apple_books.md to the above listed exact content.  �\n5828\t\n5829\t\n5830\t\n5831\t�� Request cancelled.\n5832\t\n5833\t\n5834\t\n5835\t��  > are you there?  �\n5836\t\n5837\t\n5838\t�� Yes, I am here and ready to proceed. My apologies for the delay.\n5839\t\n5840\t\n5841\t  I am about to restore the docs/apple_books.md file to the version that contains both the full ZSTATE documentation and the documentation for the fixture\n5842\t  scripts, as you requested.\n5843\t\n5844\t\n5845\t\n5846\t�� Request cancelled.\n5847\t\n5848\t\n5849\t\n5850\t��  > I have manually restored it. I have also staged all that I want to commit. Please review and prepare the commit message, which I'll review and then  �\n5851\t��  I'll approve/regect your commit  �\n5852\t\n5853\t\n5854\t�� Okay, I understand. You have manually restored docs/apple_books.md and staged all the files you wish to commit.\n5855\t\n5856\t  I will now review the staged files and then propose a commit message for your approval.\n5857\t\n5858\t\n5859\t\n5860\t�� ✔  Shell git status (Review current staged files to prepare commit message.)  �\n5861\t��  �\n5862\t��  On branch main  �\n5863\t��  Your branch is ahead of 'origin/main' by 9 commits.  �\n5864\t��  (use \"git push\" to publish your local commits)  �\n5865\t��  �\n5866\t��  Changes to be committed:  �\n5867\t��  (use \"git restore --staged <file>...\" to unstage)  �\n5868\t��  \tmodified:  TODO.md  �\n5869\t��  \tmodified:  docs/apple_books.md  �\n5870\t��  \tnew file:  specs/apple_books/fixtures/_common.sh  �\n5871\t��  \tnew file:  specs/apple_books/fixtures/copy_boo