es in CLAUDE.md are not part of this feature and\n6722\t  should be handled separately?\n6723\t\n6724\t\n6725\t��  > We'll get to that, but let's push to GH and check if the CI passes  �\n6726\t\n6727\t\n6728\t�� I can do that. I will push the changes to GitHub.\n6729\t\n6730\t\n6731\t\n6732\t�� ✔  Shell git push (Push local commits to the remote GitHub repository to trigger CI.)  �\n6733\t��  �\n6734\t��  To github.com:palimondo/BookMinder.git  �\n6735\t��  ad28f4b..14ef3da  main -> main  �\n6736\t��  �\n6737\t\n6738\t�� The changes have been pushed to GitHub. You can now check the CI run on GitHub to see if all tests pass.\n6739\t\n6740\t\n6741\t  Please let me know the results of the CI run, and we can then proceed with the next steps.\n6742\t\n6743\t\n6744\t��  > Use gh to check the CI status  �\n6745\t\n6746\t\n6747\t\n6748\t�� ✔  Shell gh run list --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,url (List the most recent GitHub Actions workflow run and get its status, conclusion, and URL.)  �\n6749\t��  �\n6750\t��  [{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/palimondo/BookMinder/actions/runs/16078517983\"}]  �\n6751\t��  �\n6752\t\n6753\t�� The most recent CI run is currently in_progress.\n6754\t\n6755\t\n6756\t  I will wait for it to complete and then check its status again.\n6757\t\n6758\t�� ✔  Shell gh run list --limit 1 --json status,conclusion,url (List the most recent GitHub Actions workflow run and get its status, conclusion, and URL.)  �\n6759\t��  �\n6760\t��  [{\"conclusion\":\"success\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/palimondo/BookMinder/actions/runs/16078517983\"}]  �\n6761\t��  �\n6762\t\n6763\t�� The CI run has completed successfully!\n6764\t\n6765\t\n6766\t  Now that the CI passes, we can proceed with the next steps. As discussed, the next logical step is to implement the cloud filtering feature.\n6767\t\n6768\t\n6769\t  I will now examine the modified files (CLAUDE.md, bookminder/apple_books/library.py, bookminder/cli.py, and specs/cli_spec.py) to understand the current\n6770\t  state and plan the implementation of the cloud filtering feature.\n6771\t\n6772\t\n6773\t  First, I'll read bookminder/apple_books/library.py to see how the list_recent_books function is currently implemented and where the cloud filtering logic\n6774\t  would fit.\n6775\t\n6776\t�� ✔  ReadFile bookminder/apple_books/library.py  �\n6777\t\n6778\t�� Okay, I see that bookminder/apple_books/library.py already has a flag parameter in list_recent_books and partially implements cloud filtering by checking for\n6779\t  ZSTATE = 3. According to our ZSTATE research, cloud books can also have ZSTATE = 6 (Cloud Sample).\n6780\t\n6781\t\n6782\t  My plan is to:\n6783\t   1. Modify bookminder/apple_books/library.py to include ZSTATE = 6 when filtering by the \"cloud\" flag.\n6784\t   2. Add a new test case in specs/cli_spec.py to verify that both ZSTATE = 3 and ZSTATE = 6 books are returned when the --flag cloud is used.\n6785\t   3. Ensure bookminder/cli.py correctly passes the flag argument.\n6786\t\n6787\t\n6788\t  Let's start by modifying bookminder/apple_books/library.py. I will change the if flag == \"cloud\" condition to include ZSTATE = 6.\n6789\t\n6790\t�� -  Edit bookminder/apple_books/library.py:  if flag == \"cloud\"... =>  if flag == \"cloud\"...  �\n6791\t\n6792\t$ pytest --spec\n6793\t\n6794\t�� ============================= test session starts ==============================\n6795\t  platform darwin -- Python 3.13.5, pytest-8.3.5, pluggy-1.6.0\n6796\t  rootdir: /Users/palimondo/Developer/BookMinder\n6797\t  configfile: pytest.ini\n6798\t  testpaths: specs\n6799\t  plugins: describe-2.2.0, spec-4.0.0, cov-6.1.1\n6800\t  collected 14 items\n6801\t\n6802\t  specs/apple_books/library_spec.py:\n6803\t\n6804\t  Find book by title:\n6805\t�� It finds book by exact title\n6806\t�� It returns none when book not found\n6807\t\n6808\t  List books:\n6809\t�� It finds books from apple books directory\n6810\t�� It includes basic metadata for each book\n6811\t\n6812\t  List recent books:\n6813\t�� It returns books with reading progress\n6814\t\n6815\t  specs/cli_spec.py:\n6816\t\n6817\t  Bookminder list recent command:\n6818\t�� It shows recently read books with progress\n6819\t\n6820\t  Bookminder list recent with user parameter:\n6821\t�� It handles user who never opened apple books\n6822\t�� It handles fresh apple books user with no books\n6823\t�� It handles user with legacy apple books installation\n6824\t�� It shows books for user with reading progress\n6825\t�� It handles user with corrupted apple books database\n6826\t�� It handles non existent relative user path\n6827\t\n6828\t  Bookminder list with flag filter:\n6829\t�� It shows only cloud books when flag is cloud\n6830\t    » It shows only local books when flag is local\n6831\t\n6832\t  ======================== 13 passed, 1 skipped in 0.36s =========================\n6833\t\n6834\t\n6835\t��  > What does the above tell you?  �\n6836\t\n6837\t\n6838\t�� The output tells me that all currently implemented tests are passing, and one test is skipped. This confirms that the codebase is in a stable state.\n6839\t\n6840\t\n6841\t  Specifically, the it_shows_only_cloud_books_when_flag_is_cloud test is passing, which is directly related to the cloud filtering feature we are working on.\n6842\t\n6843\t\n6844\t  My next step is to modify bookminder/apple_books/library.py to include ZSTATE = 6 in the cloud filter, as our research indicated that ZSTATE = 6 also\n6845\t  represents cloud samples. After that, I will add a new test case to specs/cli_spec.py to ensure this change works as expected.\n6846\t\n6847\t  Here's the proposed change to bookminder/apple_books/library.py:\n6848\t\n6849\t\n6850\t\n6851\t�� ✔  Edit bookminder/apple_books/library.py:  if flag == \"cloud\"... =>  if flag == \"cloud\"...  �\n6852\t��  �\n6853\t��  119  �\n6854\t��  120  params = []  �\n6855\t��  121  if flag == \"cloud\":  �\n6856\t�